FAQ = [
 ("What is the roof load limit on a 2019–2024 Forester?",
  "Press coverage of the Wilderness launch gives the standard Forester's rails a 176 lb dynamic (driving) limit and a 700 lb static (parked) limit. The 2022–2024 Wilderness raised those to 220 lb dynamic and 800 lb static with its ladder-type rails. The dynamic figure covers the crossbars and everything on them while moving. Check the owner's manual for your exact car, and plan around the lower figure if the two ever disagree."),
 ("Do standard Forester crossbars fit the Forester Wilderness?",
  "Not the ones on this page. The Snailfly and Tuyoung titles say \"except Wilderness\" and \"not Wilderness,\" because the 2022–2024 Wilderness uses a different ladder-type rail. etrailer's fit guide treats the Wilderness as its own roof configuration. For a Wilderness, buy a Thule or Yakima raised-rail system entered in the fit guide as \"Wilderness,\" or an Amazon set whose title names the Forester Wilderness."),
 ("Can I put a rooftop tent on a Forester?",
  "The numbers allow it with care. The standard SK Forester's roof is rated at 700 lb parked, and the Wilderness at 800 lb. The limit that decides which tent you can carry is the driving one: 176 lb on standard trims and 220 lb on the Wilderness, and that includes the bars. SubaruForester.org has owner threads asking which crossbars to use for tents on the Wilderness. Choose a tent the maker approves for the Forester, and stronger bars than the cheapest set."),
 ("Do 2014–2018 Forester crossbars fit a 2019–2024?",
  "Some Amazon sets are sold as one part for both: the Snailfly and EZREXPM bars are titled 2014–2024, and the Tuyoung 2014–2026. That works because they clamp around raised rails rather than bolting to fixed points. Name-brand systems usually use vehicle-specific pads or clamps, so check the fit guide for your model year rather than reusing old parts. The 2025 Forester is a new generation, so treat it separately."),
 ("Does the Forester have bare-roof versions?",
  "Most SK Foresters have raised side rails, and our vehicle data lists them as standard. etrailer's 2022 fit guide also lists a non-Wilderness configuration \"with no existing rails or crossbars.\" If your roof has no rails, none of the raised-rail bars here will work; you'd need a clamp-to-door-jamb system from Thule or Yakima. Look before you order: raised rails stand clear of the roof with a gap underneath."),
 ("Do I need locking crossbars?",
  "Lockable bars keep a thief from unclamping the bars, and whatever is mounted to them, with a hex key. The Tuyoung and the 300 lb adjustable set are lockable according to their titles. The Snailfly and EZREXPM titles don't mention locks. If your Forester sits at trailheads or on the street, the lock cores are worth the small price difference. Lock the accessories too; a locked bar doesn't stop someone taking a bike off it."),
 ("How far apart should the crossbars be on a Forester?",
  "Clamp-on bars slide along the raised rail, so you set the spread. Cargo boxes and tents publish a minimum and maximum spread; bike and kayak mounts are more stable with more. Keep the rear bar clear of the point where the rail curves down toward the liftgate, and check that the open liftgate clears any box. Tighten evenly, then recheck the clamps after the first drive."),
 ("Which crossbars are quietest on the Forester?",
  "Aero or teardrop aluminum bars are quieter than square or round steel bars. The Rack Shop says Yakima's teardrop JetStream bars cut wind noise better than its steel CoreBar, and etrailer offers Thule's WingBar Evo aero bar for the Forester at $544.90. The flush Thule WingBar Edge and Yakima TimberLine FX sit within the rails and look cleaner. Whatever you buy, avoid long overhang and keep the end caps on. Bars off between trips is quietest."),
 ("Can I open the moonroof with crossbars installed?",
  "etrailer attaches a note to the Thule systems it fits to the Forester: it is not recommended to open, vent or retract the sun, moon or glass roof while the product is installed. A loaded bar or accessory can sit close to the glass panel's path. If your Forester has a moonroof, treat that as the rule for any rack, not just Thule's."),
 ("Are cheap Amazon crossbars safe on a Forester?",
  "The ones here are titled for the Forester's raised rails and state a bar rating, which is the minimum you should accept. What they lack compared with Thule or Yakima is a published fit guide, a warranty you can read in advance and a large accessory range. For a cargo bag, skis or a bike tray kept under the 176 lb driving limit, they're a reasonable buy. For a tent or daily use, the name-brand systems etrailer lists are the safer choice."),
]

